\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. When I survey the wondrous Cross
\par On which the Prince of Glory died,
\par My richest gain I count but loss,
\par And pour contempt on all my pride.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Forbid it, Lord, that I should boast,
\par Save in the death of Christ, my God:
\par All the vain things that charm me most,
\par I sacrificee them to His blood.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. See, from His head, His hands, His feet,
\par Sorrow and love flow mingled down:
\par Did e'er such love and sorrow meet,
\par Or thorns compose so rich a crown?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Were the whole realm of nature mine,
\par That were an offering far too small;
\par Love so amazing, so divine,
\par Demands my soul, my life, my all.\f1 
\par 
\par }

